{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nJapan stole my heart in just five days. Our journey began in Tokyo, where neon lights and towering skyscrapers met centuries-old temples. We wandered through **Shibuya Crossing**, the world’s busiest pedestrian intersection, then escaped to the serene gardens of **Meiji Shrine**. The city’s energy was intoxicating—sushi at **Tsukiji Outer Market**, matcha desserts in **Asakusa**, and the quiet hum of a **capsule hotel** at night.\n\nNext, we sped to **Kyoto**, a city frozen in time. Cherry blossoms lined the **Philosopher’s Path**, and traditional **ryokan** (inns) offered private onsen baths under the stars. We sipped **matcha** in bamboo groves, bowed to **Fushimi Inari’s** thousands of red torii gates, and got lost in the maze-like alleys of **Gion**. The contrast between Kyoto’s delicate kimonos and the futuristic **Arashiyama Monkey Park** was pure magic.\n\nOur final stop was **Osaka**, the food lover’s paradise. We devoured **takoyaki** (octopus balls) and **okonomiyaki** (savory pancakes) before boarding the **Shinkansen** (bullet train) back to Tokyo. The efficiency of Japan’s trains—clean, punctual, and breathtakingly scenic—left us in awe.\n\nJapan is a land of extremes: ancient meets modern, silence meets chaos, tradition meets innovation. And in just a week, I fell hopelessly in love. Already plotting my return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -0.8805687427520752}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.08243269473314285}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.005001414567232132}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -0.11066357791423798